// Workspace type-check config (Story 1.3 QA — closes the type-assertion gap).
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS:
//   The production build (`pnpm -r build` → per-package `tsc -b`) and the test
//   runner (`pnpm test` → Vitest/esbuild) BOTH skip type-checking the co-located
//   `*.test.ts` files:
//     - tsconfig.base.json `exclude`s `**/*.test.ts` from every package build, so
//       `tsc -b` never sees them.
//     - Vitest transforms via esbuild WITHOUT type-checking and has no `typecheck`
//       runner configured, so `expectTypeOf(...)` / `@ts-expect-error` in tests are
//       runtime NO-OPS — a deliberately wrong type assertion still passes.
//   Result: every type-level guarantee asserted in a test (e.g. EventPayloadMap
//   totality — that every EventType has a payload — which is enforced ONLY by the
//   compile-time `extends Record<EventType, object>` constraint, and the
//   `@ts-expect-error` closed-vocabulary / closed-error-code guards) was VACUOUS in
//   the default suite and in CI.
//
// WHAT THIS DOES:
//   A single, non-composite, `noEmit` pass that type-checks ALL workspace source
//   AND test files (it does NOT inherit the base `exclude`, so tests ARE checked).
//   Driven by the root `typecheck` script and wired as a hard CI gate, so the
//   test files' type assertions finally fail the run when they are wrong.
//
//   Kept as a SEPARATE config (not folded into the package builds) so the shipped
//   `dist` stays test-free and the "packages never redefine the root config"
//   convention is preserved — this is one root config, like vitest.config.ts.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": false,
    // Node globals (`import.meta.url`, `node:*` builtins) are used by some test
    // files (e.g. the Story 1.2 boundary-enforcement test). Vitest's
    // expectTypeOf/assertType helpers resolve from the explicit `vitest` import,
    // so they need no ambient types entry here.
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  // Override the base `exclude` (which drops **/*.test.ts) so test files ARE
  // type-checked here. Only skip dependencies / build output.
  "exclude": ["**/node_modules/**", "**/dist/**"],
  "include": [
    "packages/*/src/**/*.ts",
    "packages/*/src/**/*.tsx",
    "apps/*/src/**/*.ts",
    "apps/*/src/**/*.tsx"
  ]
}
